    "content": "For the 2026 Masters, official lottery tickets (patron applications) were priced at $125 for Monday/Tuesday practice rounds, $150 for Wednesday's Par 3 Contest, and $160 per day for tournament rounds (Thursday–Sunday). Lottery winners are notified in July to pay these face-value prices, which are significantly lower than third-party reseller sites. Masters Lottery Ticket Prices (2026 Official) Practice Rounds (Mon/Tue): $125 Practice Round (Wed - Par 3): $150 Tournament Days (Thu-Sun): $160 4-Day Tournament Badge: $525 Key Details for 2027 Applicants Application Window: Tickets for the 2027 Masters will be available on Masters.com when the application window opens on June 1, 2026. Masters.com Cost & Value: These prices are the lowest available; secondary market tickets can cost thousands per day. Payment: Winners are notified by email in late July and must supply payment at that time. Restriction: It is highly recommended to use the official site, as third-party tickets can be canceled. Note: Prices are subject to change for the 2027 tournament, following a $20 increase in 2026.",
